{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is implicated in the regulation of NCI-H446 through a series of target relationships that converge on the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a common target for multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine, Methyl valerate, and Pseudopterosin Q, all of which are linked to NCI-H446. The evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- may exert its effects by modulating the proteasome complex, which is involved in protein degradation and cellular homeostasis. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles indicates a potential mechanism of action that involves the proteasome, possibly through the regulation of specific subunits. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the proteasome in the biological response to Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and its potential relevance to NCI-H446.",
